-- `main_a.mdk` with the two import lines swapped: `b` is loaded BEFORE `a`,
-- and the prop is still over `a`'s `Color`, so the draw must still come from
-- `a`'s instance -- every case is `Red`.
--
-- WHICH type a prop is over and WHICH order the two modules were imported in
-- are two independent questions, and one is not evidence about the other: a
-- candidate list keyed on the shared route word is built in load order, so a
-- fix that takes the first candidate rather than the resolved type's own is
-- right here and wrong in `main_a.mdk` (or the reverse). The four entries are
-- the SET that tells those apart.
import b
import a.{Color(..), tag}

prop "a's own Arbitrary instance is what a's Color draws from" (c : Color) =
  tag c == "a-red"
